    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0177" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.60f11/25</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Czechoslovak Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Beneš</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Prague</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-24"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received December
                        3.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: The keen desire which
                    animates the Government of the Czechoslovak Republic to continue and strengthen
                    the friendly relations which have been built up between the United States of
                    North America and the Czechoslovak Republic has prompted it to create a
                    diplomatic post near that [<hi rendition="#italic">your</hi>] Government. Mr.
                    Jan Masaryk, a Counselor of Legation, is therefore charged with the duty of
                    placing in your hands these credentials which accredit him to the [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">your</hi>] Government as a Chargé d’Affaires <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad interim</hi>, until the Government of the Republic
                    shall be in a position <pb facs="0178" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/> to appoint its
                    Minister Plenipotentiary near the Government of the United States of North
                    America.</p>
                <p>The talent and conciliatory spirit of that diplomatic agent warrant my hope that
                    you will receive him kindly and that you will give faith and credit to all the
                    communications he may send to you within his instructions which will mainly aim
                    to seek the means best adopted [<hi rendition="#italic">adapted</hi>] to
                    strengthening and developing the relations between our two countries.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dr. Eduard Benes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
